STEP-2 RESULT + SESSION-13 SYNTHESIS
==============================================================================
STEP 2 (static-vs-dynamic): NO DYNAMIC SIGNATURE. The confound-free differential
(capture slope - static-model slope, same chain so Gpost/treble/clipper cancel) is
~0 at every tone, and the below-corner 110 Hz (mean |dev| 0.07) is NOT anomalous vs
the above-corner tones (0.11). The dense 1 kHz ladder shows the static model tracking
the capture's H2-vs-level to ~0.5 dB over 30 dB. => The capture's JFET H2-vs-level is
STATIC-CONSISTENT; the C3 degeneration-bypass does NOT introduce a memory effect the
static shelf+shaper misses. LEAN: STATIC (caveat: below-corner = one frequency, thin).

CROSS-CHECK with STEP 1 (phase), and why they are consistent:
  * Step 2 says a STATIC shaper CAN fit. Step 1 says the CURRENT (session-11-fitted)
    ceiling odd term does NOT match the capture's H3 phase (55-166 deg off, freq-dep).
    These agree: the static FAMILY is adequate, but the current ceiling ODD-TERM SHAPE
    is wrong (magnitude and possibly sign). A static real nonlinearity can only make H3
    at intrinsic 0/180 deg (times downstream linear phase); the capture being ~180 from
    the model at 1 kHz = the ceiling odd term is BACKWARDS there, a STATIC sign fix.
  * Step 1's freq-dependent verdict (ceiling-right at 220/440, backwards at 1000) is,
    under the static conclusion, LINEAR-MODEL phase error (the mismodelled 717 Hz
    bridged-T notch corrupts 220's H3 at 660 Hz) — NOT genuine intrinsic freq-dependence
    (a static nonlinearity cannot have that). So down-weight 220 in any phase-aware fit.

BRANCH DECISION (handover §3o(3)):
  Static is NOT contradicted => the indicated path is the STATIC branch:
    reshape the JFET ceiling's ODD-LIMITING term, fitted against COMPLEX (phase-aware)
    targets, with a §3j-style discriminating check BEFORE any fit, and dsp-validator
    (Opus, high) sign-off on the JfetStage.h change (monotonicity, ADAA-preserving
    antiderivative, existing odd-part/H3-zero/DC-step tests).
  NOT the expensive coupled-Newton JFET rewrite — no dynamic evidence supports it.

DE-RISK BEFORE COMMITTING (pre-authorised, user decision — a capture, not code):
  ONE capture: drive-min level ladder at 110 AND 220 Hz, 3 dB steps, extending BELOW
  -36 dBFS. Gives dense clipper-free H2-vs-level slope curves at a below-corner and an
  on-corner frequency to overlay against the 1 kHz ladder and CONFIRM static before the
  branch commit. The below-corner static evidence currently rests on 3 slope samples at
  one frequency; this capture removes that thinness. Cheap; nothing else new is needed.

TRAPS FOUND THIS SESSION (both are in the plan's own recipe — keep flagged):
  1. 'ceiling-only via high clipSat' (§3o step 1) is INVALID: the D1/D2 clamp window
     tracks satLo (Clipper.h clampHi=9.6-satLo), so clipSat>~10 freezes node W into a DC
     source and the residual output is the harmonic-free clean BLEND bleed. Use coherent
     complex subtraction of valid renders instead (done).
  2. Raw A_eff-collapse (only Gpre) is confounded by the treble net + clipper AFTER the
     JFET, which a STATIC model shares — so raw non-collapse is NOT a dynamic signature.
     The differential-vs-static-model is the confound-free test (done).
